--- how this capture was taken ---
Fresh Chromium process and a fresh browser context, so nothing was served from
an HTTP cache, from storage or from a warm service worker. Navigation to
https://chat-hive.scubed.co/ only; every hop after that is the deployment's own
OAUTH_AUTO_REDIRECT carrying the browser through OIDC. The run stops when the
sign-in form's submit control is visible, resolved by accessible role rather
than by selector. Chromium was launched through the SOCKS proxy at
127.0.0.1:1080, which this development host needs to reach Cloudflare at all.

--- what this before capture shows ---
The /oauth/consent hop answers 200 with a rendered document rather than a
redirect, and the navigation to /auth/sign-in follows roughly two seconds
later: the consent panel is booting in the browser, reading the session,
finding none, and navigating to a URL the server could have named without
painting anything. That gap is the subject of issue #967 and the reason the
sign-in journey misses the p90 target in issue #945.

--- redaction ---
authorization_id, code_challenge, client_id, state and nonce are masked in this
log and in the screenshot's URL banner before upload. The banner is drawn into
the page by the capture script, so the masked value is what reaches the pixels;
nothing scans an uploaded image.
